# TeamVault, the README flow as requests. Run top to bottom in the IntelliJ HTTP client;
# the login and create requests store what later requests need. Needs the app on 8080
# (./mvnw spring-boot:run -Dspring-boot.run.profiles=dev) and the dev seed (devpass12).

@host = http://localhost:8080
@acme = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@globex = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222

### ping (public)
GET {{host}}/api/ping

### register carol (201, no token: tokens come from login only; run twice for the 409)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "carol@example.com", "password": "correct-horse-battery", "displayName": "Carol"}

### login as carol, keep the token
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "carol@example.com", "password": "correct-horse-battery"}

> {% client.global.set("carol", response.body.token); %}

### who am I
GET {{host}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer {{carol}}

### found Initech: the creator becomes its first ADMIN, keep the id
POST {{host}}/api/companies
Authorization: Bearer {{carol}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Initech", "tier": "SMALL"}

> {% client.global.set("initech", response.body.id); %}

### add bob as MEMBER (ADMIN only)
POST {{host}}/api/companies/{{initech}}/members
  Authorization: Bearer {{carol}}
  Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "bob@globex.example"}

### Initech members
GET {{host}}/api/companies/{{initech}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{carol}}

### login as alice (Acme ADMIN), keep the token
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "alice@acme.example", "password": "devpass12"}

> {% client.global.set("alice", response.body.token); %}

### upload into Acme (run twice for the 409 duplicate filename)
POST {{host}}/api/companies/{{acme}}/files
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="hello.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

Hello from the HTTP client
--WebAppBoundary--

### list Acme files, newest first
GET {{host}}/api/companies/{{acme}}/files
  Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}

### alice's companies with her role in each
GET {{host}}/api/companies
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}

### login as bob (Globex MEMBER, Initech MEMBER), keep the token
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "bob@globex.example", "password": "devpass12"}

> {% client.global.set("bob", response.body.token); %}

### error: no token, 401 authentication-required with WWW-Authenticate: Bearer
GET {{host}}/api/companies/{{acme}}/files

### error: garbage token, 401 invalid-token
GET {{host}}/api/companies/{{acme}}/files
Authorization: Bearer not.a.jwt

### error: bob is not an Acme member, 403 membership-required
GET {{host}}/api/companies/{{acme}}/files
Authorization: Bearer {{bob}}

### error: bob is MEMBER at Initech, adding someone needs ADMIN, 403 admin-role-required
POST {{host}}/api/companies/{{initech}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{bob}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "alice@acme.example"}

### error: wrong password, 401 bad-credentials (same body as an unknown email)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
  Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "alice@acme.example", "password": "nope"}

### error: blank name, 400 validation-failed with the errors list
POST {{host}}/api/companies
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "  ", "tier": "SMALL"}

### error: unknown tier, 400 malformed-body
POST {{host}}/api/companies
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Hooli", "tier": "HUGE"}

### error: unknown route with a valid token, 404 without type (about:blank)
GET {{host}}/api/nope
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}

### the contract (public in every profile); the UI is at /swagger-ui.html in dev only
GET {{host}}/v3/api-docs.yaml